    description: "## Decision to write down (as docs/adr/0062-*.md)\nA live-document layer for the tracker: a Yjs document (CRDT) that is a **projection of, and an edit buffer over, the ops log** -- never a replacement for it. The ops log (.ops files, flock, Lamport clocks, journal; ADR-0013) stays the durable, authoritative layer; the Y.Doc is the live, multi-writer buffer. This is the same split PlazaFlow's spec draws (\"Git is the durability layer, the CRDT is the live collaboration buffer\"), and the experiment is the PlazaFlow v0.1-v0.2 rehearsal (sync, persistence, awareness; encryption later) with the BlockSuite dependency removed -- what transfers is Yjs, per ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_10162026_2318.md section 4.\n\n## What the ADR must decide\n1. Y.Doc shape: items as Y.Map<id, Y.Map of fields>; discussion as Y.Array of Y.Map entries whose body is a Y.Text; which fields are live-editable in the doc (candidates: discussion drafts, description, title) vs op-only (status, priority, tags, parent, isbefore, locks, edit-mode -- these keep going through Store ops so validation and governance apply).\n2. Authority on conflict: an op's projection always wins; a live edit becomes real only when the bridge emits an op (see the write-back item).\n3. Attribution: every live change carries a **pseudonymous token** (Yjs clientID or per-session id); the token -> author (`by:`) resolution table is kept OUT of the shared doc. Rehearses PlazaFlow §4.8/§12.1 (attribution withheld from content readers) and avoids the leak PlazaFlow's §4.8.2 had.\n4. Awareness schema: {item_id in view, client label, kind: human|agent}.\n5. Transport: y-protocols sync + awareness over a WebSocket on `htrac serve` (localhost-only) vs a sidecar `y-websocket` process for the experiment. Python binding: pycrdt (0.14.10, 2026-10-19, maintained) -- y-py (0.6.2, last release 2023-10-05) is unmaintained. Yjs 13.6 vs 14 must be chosen explicitly: as of 2026-10-29 `yjs` latest is 13.6.33 (2026-09-23) and 14 is still pre-release (`yjs@14.0.0-16` beta, 2025-12-07; `@y/y` 14.0.0-rc.29 beta).\n   CONSTRAINT ON THE SERVE OPTION: `run_server` calls `create_app()` with no TrackerSet and no authenticator, so production `htrac serve` serves no tracker; wiring both is WI-pupod (owner-deferred indefinitely). Until then an endpoint inside serve is unreachable (the WI-hopip gate denies) and its watchfiles/state_snapshot loop does not run, so the experiment needs the sidecar or an in-process app wired the way the tests wire it.\n6. Security posture and non-goals: 127.0.0.1 only until WI-sunan (tracker self-claims, todo_hard) lands; not multi-repo; not a replacement for `tracker sync`. WI-hopip is DONE (PR #1751): `create_app(authenticate=...)` denies every route but /health and the static mount by default (401, WS close 1008), and test_serve_auth_gate.py enumerates the app's routes -- so a Yjs sync route added to serve is inside that gate, and the ADR must say which authenticator admits it.\n## Inputs\nADR-0013, ADR-0019 (amended 2026-10-17: its frontend row already names ADR-0062 / WI-tofog, and it already carries \"Why not BlockSuite (re-decided 2026-10-17)\"), INV-hivog (two-user mode -- the existing multi-user seam), serve.py's watchfiles loop and state_snapshot broadcast (they run only when a TrackerSet is wired -- see the constraint under decision 5), store.py op kinds (create, update, discuss, discuss_clear, discuss_summarize, lock, unlock, reconcile, edit-mode-on/off). PlazaFlow spec (codeberg.org/iterabloom/pf-prelim): v0.1 §3.2/§6.2 (y-websocket + y-webrtc as scaffolding), v1.2 §4.8 (attribution model), v0.2 encryption.\n## Done when\nThe ADR is merged with the six decisions recorded. \"Why not BlockSuite\" is already recorded in ADR-0019 (re-decided 2026-10-17); ADR-0062 cites it rather than restating it."  # fa65
- op: discuss  # bff5
