  message: "CORRECTION to the note above: codeberg.org IS on ALLOWED_WEBSITES.md, so the pf-prelim citations are now checked (repo iterabloom/pf-prelim, default branch dev, last updated 2026-04-08; files under docs/spec/ and docs/spec/will-implement-later-and-not-now/). All hold: v0.1 §3.2 'Relay Architecture' and §6.2 'y-websocket + y-webrtc as Scaffolding' exist; the v0.2 encryption is §6.1 'Fragment-Keyed Encryption'; v1.2 §4.8 'Attribution Model' exists, and §4.8.2 is the leak the item names -- it stores meta:createdBy / meta:updatedBy public keys inside the shared Yjs doc (via BlockSuite), readable by every content reader; v1.2 §4.8.5 names clientID leakage and requires the clientID->keypair map never travel in plaintext, which is decision 3's out-of-doc token map; v1.2 §12.1 'Fragment-Keyed Encryption' puts attribution under its own DEK, the 'withheld from content readers' reading. Not compared: ~/plazaflow/spec.md (2026-03-15) against these files."  # 806f
