- op: discuss  # 20eb
  at: '2026-10-29T19:49:02Z'  # 20eb
  by: agent  # 20eb
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 20eb
  clock: 9  # 20eb
  nonce: 20eb  # 20eb
  message: "Done: PR #1943 (dev 00e944eab4) merged docs/adr/0062-tracker-live-document-layer.md, Status: Accepted, indexed in docs/adr/README.md. The six decisions: (1) one Y.Doc per tracker root; live-editable only title, description and a per-client draft discussion entry, each committing as its existing op; status/priority/tags/links/fields/locked_fields/frozen/posted entries op-only plain values; stealth tier not projected. (2) ops log wins; bridge emits ops through TrackerSet/Store only; commit on 5 s idle or explicit post; an op superseding uncommitted live text notifies the editor, no silent re-apply. (3) pseudonymous clientID in the doc, token->by/actor table in the server process filled at authenticated handshake, unknown tokens refused. (4) awareness = {item_id, server-assigned pseudonym label, kind}. (5) Yjs 13.6 + pycrdt 0.14.10 + pycrdt-websocket 0.16.5 on a /yjs route inside create_app's WI-hopip guard; Node y-websocket sidecar rejected; dependency on WI-pupod stated, not raised. (6) 127.0.0.1 until WI-sunan; no encryption (WI-pufun); not federation; not a tracker-sync replacement. 'Why not BlockSuite' cited from ADR-0019. Also corrects my earlier op-kind note: the message-editing ops delete-msg / undelete-msg / edit-msg-text (inside human edit-mode windows) exist too; the ADR keeps them out of the live doc."  # 20eb
